<title>USA: TABLE - Nike Q4 shr $0.52 vs $0.45.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Nike Q4 shr $0.52 vs $0.45.</headline>
<dateline>BEAVERTON, Ore. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>NIKE, INC.	 QUARTER ENDING		  Y-T-D ENDING</p>
<p>    QTR FINL STMT  5/31/97	5/31/96*	5/31/97 5/31/96*  REVENUES	  $2,373,931  $1,852,067 $9,186,539 $6,470,625</p>
<p>COSTS &amp; EXPENSES</p>
<p>   COST OF SALES  1,427,819   1,120,553  5,502,993  3,906,746</p>
<p>   SG&amp;A		 666,135     497,703  2,303,704  1,588,612</p>
<p>   INTEREST EXP	  18,853	 4,929    52,343    39,498</p>
<p>   OTHER		   10,870	11,455    32,277    36,679</p>
<p>     TOTAL COSTS  2,123,677   1,634,640  7,891,317  5,571,535</p>
<p> PRE TAX		  250,254     217,427  1,295,222  899,090</p>
<p> TAXES		     94,500	83,700   499,400   345,900</p>
<p> NET INCOME	     155,754     133,727   795,822   553,190</p>
<p> INCOME PER SHARE	  0.52	  0.45	2.68	1.88</p>
<p> DIVIDEND		    0.10	  0.08	0.38	0.29</p>
<p> NUMBER OF SHARES     297,252     295,466   297,000   293,608</p>
<p>NOTE: Future orders, scheduled for delivery between June</p>
<p>and November 1997, are $4.9 billion, 18 percent higher than</p>
<p>such orders for the same period last year. Had the U.S. dollar</p>
<p>remained constant worldwide futures orders would have risen by</p>
<p>22 percent.</p>
<p>Note - Q4 gross margin 39.9 pct vs 39.5 yr ago.</p>
</text>
